{"id":"u-f53d7a69-b1ee-4502-8223-84aad160740a","src":"community","title":"Custom PPL","author":"James K.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/0MQJj0-custom-ppl","desc":"The original Reddit PPL (Push/Pull/Legs) program is a popular linear progression routine, often praised for its balance of strength and hypertrophy. To optimize it for powerlifting, the focus shifts more heavily towards the three main powerlifts: Squat, Bench Press, and Deadlift. This involves increasing their frequency, prioritizing lower rep ranges for strength gains, and selecting accessory exercises that directly support these lifts.\n\nHere's a modified Reddit PPL program optimized for powerlifting, maintaining the 6-day split:\n\nKey Principles of this Powerlifting-Optimized PPL:\n\n    Increased Frequency of Main Lifts: Squat, Bench Press, and Deadlift are trained more often, with variations.\n    Strength Focus (Lower Reps): The primary compound movements will predominantly use lower rep ranges to build maximal strength.\n    Volume & Intensity Cycling: While linear progression is still the backbone, some days will be heavier/lower rep, and others will be lighter/higher rep to manage fatigue and accumulate volume.\n    Accessory Work for Weak Points: Accessories are chosen to directly improve the main lifts or address common weak points in powerlifters.\n    Ample Rest for Main Lifts: Longer rest periods between sets for the main lifts are crucial for recovery and performance.\n    Progressive Overload: Continue to add weight to the bar consistently. When you hit the top of the rep range for a given weight, increase the weight in the next session.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Strength","Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-03-14T16:51:44.073Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Pull (Heavy Deadlift Focus)","Push (Heavy Bench Focus)","Legs (Heavy Squat Focus)","Pull (Volume Back Focus)","Legs (Volume Squat Variation F","Push (Volume/Technique Bench F"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":3,"hi":5,"rpe":7},{"lo":3,"hi":5,"rpe":8}],"note":"Traditional or Sumo"},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"Narrow Grip"},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"Alternatives are preacher curl or regular dumbbell curls"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8,"x":4}],"note":"Focus on heavy, clean reps.\nProgression: Add 5 lbs when all sets are completed."},{"n":"Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}],"note":"Controlled on eccentric and concentric"},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"Rope or Bar"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":3,"hi":5,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"Focus on heavy, clean reps\nProgression: Add 10 lbs when all sets are completed."},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"Hamstring and glute development, lower back support for squat/deadlift"},{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"Alternative is Front Squat"},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":6,"x":3}],"note":"Lower RPE, higher volume."},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}],"note":"or Pull-Ups if possible\nFocus on slow & controlled"},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"Wide Grip"},{"n":"Reverse Pec Deck","sets":[{"lo